.TH git-scan-unicode 1
.SH NAME
git-scan-unicode \- detect dangerous Unicode characters in a diff
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git scan-unicode
[\fB\-\-staged\fR|\fB\-\-worktree\fR|\fIrev-range\fR]
[\fB\-\-warn\-only\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-color\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Scans lines added by a diff for Unicode characters that make the rendered text
disagree with what a compiler reads, as used by the Trojan Source attacks
(CVE-2021-42574 and CVE-2021-42694).
.PP
Bidirectional controls, line/paragraph separators, C0/C1 controls and invisible
formatting characters outside emoji sequences are reported as BLOCK. Text that
is not NFC-normalised and confusable mixed-script words are reported as WARN.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
No findings.
.TP
.B 1
WARN findings only.
.TP
.B 2
At least one BLOCK finding.
.TP
.B 3
Usage error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B git scan-unicode --staged
Check before committing.
.TP
.B git scan-unicode ORIG_HEAD..HEAD
Check what a merge just brought in.
.SH SEE ALSO
.UR https://trojansource.codes/
.UE
